.TH CATQ 1 "@PROJECT_VERSION@" "@PROJECT_AUTHOR@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
catq \- concatenate files and print on standard output (quiet on missing files)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B catq
[\fIOPTION\fR]... [\fIFILE\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B catq
concatenates
.I FILE(s)
to standard output.
With no
.I FILE,
or when
.I FILE
is \-,
read standard input.
.PP
Unlike
.BR cat (1),
.B catq
silently ignores missing files without printing an error message.
This is useful when you want to concatenate multiple files but some may not exist.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-show\-all
equivalent to \-vET
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-number\-nonblank
number nonempty output lines, overrides \-n
.TP
.BR \-e
equivalent to \-vE
.TP
.BR \-E ", " \-\-show\-ends
display $ at end of each line
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-number
number all output lines
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-squeeze\-blank
suppress repeated empty output lines
.TP
.BR \-t
equivalent to \-vT
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-show\-tabs
display TAB characters as ^I
.TP
.BR \-u
(ignored)
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-show\-nonprinting
use ^ and M- notation, except for LFD and TAB
.TP
.B \-\-help
display this help and exit
.TP
.B \-\-version
output version information and exit
.SH EXAMPLES
Concatenate files, silently skipping missing ones:
.PP
.nf
catq file1.txt file2.txt file3.txt > combined.txt
.fi
.PP
Display file with line numbers:
.PP
.nf
catq \-n notes.txt
.fi
.PP
Show non-printing characters:
.PP
.nf
catq \-A data.bin
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Usage error or out of memory.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LANGUAGE
.TQ
.B LC_ALL
.TQ
.B LC_MESSAGES
.TQ
.B LANG
Select the language for messages and translated man pages when available.
